#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to transpiling quantum circuits in the Qiskit SDK."
msgstr "Pengantar untuk melakukan transpilasi sirkuit kuantum menggunakan Qiskit SDK."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to transpilation"
msgstr "Pengantar transpilasi"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to transpilation {#introduction-to-transpilation}"
msgstr "Pengantar transpilasi {#introduction-to-transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An overview of transpilation and the relevant tools to use, either locally or in the cloud.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/transpile-intro.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran umum transpilasi dan alat-alat yang relevan, baik secara lokal maupun di cloud.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/transpile-intro.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Transpilation is the process of rewriting a given input circuit to match the topology of a specific quantum device, and optimize the circuit instructions for execution on noisy quantum computers.  This documentation covers the tooling and workflows for local transpilation available to all Qiskit users.  If you're using primitives and are only interested in the default transpilation options provided by the Qiskit Runtime service, read the [Configure runtime compilation for Qiskit Runtime](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) topic.\n"
msgid "Transpilation is the process of rewriting a given input circuit to match the topology of a specific quantum device, and optimize the circuit instructions for execution on noisy quantum computers.  This documentation covers the tooling and workflows for local transpilation available to all Qiskit users.  If you're using primitives and are only interested in the default transpilation options provided by IBM Quantum Compute Service, read the [Error mitigation and suppression techniques](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) topic.\n"
msgstr "Transpilasi adalah proses penulisan ulang sirkuit masukan agar sesuai dengan topologi perangkat kuantum tertentu, serta mengoptimalkan instruksi sirkuit untuk eksekusi pada komputer kuantum yang bising. Dokumentasi ini mencakup alat dan alur kerja untuk transpilasi lokal yang tersedia bagi semua pengguna Qiskit. Kalau kamu menggunakan primitives dan hanya tertarik pada opsi transpilasi default yang disediakan oleh layanan Qiskit Runtime, baca topik [Configure runtime compilation for Qiskit Runtime](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The process of transpilation takes a circuit that contains your instructions:\n"
msgstr "Proses transpilasi mengambil sebuah sirkuit yang berisi instruksimu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A two-qubit quantum circuit containing a Hadamard and two CNOT gates.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/pre-transpiled.avif \"Quantum circuit\")\n"
msgstr "![Sirkuit kuantum dua-Qubit yang berisi gerbang Hadamard dan dua gerbang CNOT.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/pre-transpiled.avif \"Quantum circuit\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation then transforms it such that only instructions available on a chosen backend are used, and optimizes those instructions to minimize the effects of noise:\n"
msgstr "Transpilasi kemudian mengubahnya sehingga hanya instruksi yang tersedia pada Backend yang dipilih yang digunakan, dan mengoptimalkan instruksi tersebut untuk meminimalkan efek noise:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The same two-qubit quantum circuit after transpilation.  It contains RZ, X, SX, and ECR gates.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/transpiled.avif \"Quantum circuit after transpilation\")\n"
msgstr "![Sirkuit kuantum dua-Qubit yang sama setelah transpilasi. Berisi gerbang RZ, X, SX, dan ECR.](/docs/images/guides/transpile/transpiled.avif \"Quantum circuit after transpilation\")\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A central component of the Qiskit SDK, the transpiler is designed for modularity and extensibility. Its main use is to write new circuit transformations (known as transpiler **passes**), and combine them with other existing passes, greatly reducing the depth and complexity of quantum circuits.  Which passes are chained together and in which order has a major effect on the final outcome. This pipeline is determined by the [`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager) and [`StagedPassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.StagedPassManager) objects.  The `StagedPassManager` orchestrates the execution of one or more `PassManagers` and determines the order in which they are executed, while the `PassManager` object is merely a collection of one or more passes.  Think of the `StagedPassManager` as the conductor in an orchestra, the `PassManagers` as the different instrument sections, and the `Pass` objects as the individual musicians.  In this way, you can compose hardware-efficient quantum circuits that let you execute utility-scale work while keeping noise manageable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find more information about the pass manager stages in the [Transpiler stages](transpiler-stages) topic.\n"
msgstr "Temukan informasi lebih lanjut tentang tahapan pass manager di topik [Transpiler stages](transpiler-stages).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction set architecture {#instruction-set-architecture}"
msgstr "Instruction set architecture {#instruction-set-architecture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to reducing the depth and complexity of quantum circuits, the transpiler is designed to transform the instructions contained in a given `QuantumCircuit` to obey the Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) of a particular backend.  Circuits obeying the ISA consist only of instructions that are supported by the backend's [`Target`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target), such as the hardware's available basis gates, measurements, resets, and control flow operations, and comply with the constraints specified by the connectivity of the hardware, that is, the target's [`CouplingMap`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap).  When submitting a job to an IBM Quantum&reg; backend, the circuits must adhere to the backend's ISA.\n"
msgstr "Selain mengurangi kedalaman dan kompleksitas sirkuit kuantum, Transpiler dirancang untuk mengubah instruksi yang terkandung dalam `QuantumCircuit` tertentu agar mematuhi Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) dari Backend tertentu. Sirkuit yang mematuhi ISA hanya terdiri dari instruksi yang didukung oleh [`Target`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) Backend, seperti basis gates yang tersedia di hardware, pengukuran, reset, dan operasi control flow, serta mematuhi batasan yang ditentukan oleh konektivitas hardware, yaitu [`CouplingMap`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) target. Saat mengirimkan job ke Backend IBM Quantum&reg;, sirkuit harus mengikuti ISA Backend tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiler stages {#transpiler-stages}"
msgstr "Tahapan Transpiler {#transpiler-stages}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit's prebuilt transpiler pipeline consists of six fundamental stages:\n"
msgstr "Pipeline Transpiler bawaan Qiskit terdiri dari enam tahap fundamental:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`init` - This pass runs any initial passes that are required before the circuit can be embedded.  This typically involves unrolling custom instructions and converting the circuit to all single- and two-qubit gates. By default, this validates the circuit instructions and translates multi-qubit gates into single- and two-qubit gates.\n"
msgstr "`init` - Pass ini menjalankan pass awal apa pun yang diperlukan sebelum sirkuit dapat di-embed. Ini biasanya melibatkan unrolling instruksi kustom dan mengonversi sirkuit ke semua gerbang single- dan two-Qubit. Secara default, ini memvalidasi instruksi sirkuit dan menerjemahkan gerbang multi-Qubit menjadi gerbang single- dan two-Qubit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`layout` - This pass applies a *layout*, mapping the virtual qubits in your circuit to the QPU's physical qubits.\n"
msgstr "`layout` - Pass ini menerapkan *layout*, memetakan qubit virtual dalam sirkuitmu ke qubit fisik QPU.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`routing` - This pass runs after a layout has been applied and will inject gates (that is, SWAPs) in the original circuit to make it compatible with the QPU's connectivity (coupling map).\n"
msgstr "`routing` - Pass ini berjalan setelah layout diterapkan dan akan menyisipkan gerbang (yaitu, SWAP) di sirkuit asli agar kompatibel dengan konektivitas QPU (coupling map).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`translation` - This pass translates the gates in the circuit to the QPU's basis set of instructions.\n"
msgstr "`translation` - Pass ini menerjemahkan gerbang dalam sirkuit ke set instruksi basis QPU.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`optimization` - This pass runs an optimization loop to find more efficient decompositions of the quantum circuit until a condition is met (such as a fixed depth).\n"
msgstr "`optimization` - Pass ini menjalankan loop optimasi untuk menemukan dekomposisi yang lebih efisien dari sirkuit kuantum sampai suatu kondisi terpenuhi (seperti kedalaman tetap).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`scheduling` - This stage is for any hardware-aware scheduling passes. If the user specifies a scheduling method, this stage accounts for all idle time in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "`scheduling` - Tahap ini untuk pass penjadwalan yang sadar hardware. Jika pengguna menentukan metode penjadwalan, tahap ini memperhitungkan semua waktu idle dalam sirkuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid " If you customize a transpilation workflow, use these stages as a guideline during development.\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu menyesuaikan alur kerja transpilasi, gunakan tahap-tahap ini sebagai panduan selama pengembangan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile with pass managers {#transpile-with-pass-managers}"
msgstr "Transpilasi dengan pass manager {#transpile-with-pass-managers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The recommended way to transpile a circuit is to create a staged pass manager and then execute its `run` method with your circuit as input. You can use the [`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager#qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager) function to generate a staged pass manager with reasonable defaults.\n"
msgstr "Cara yang disarankan untuk melakukan transpilasi pada sebuah sirkuit adalah dengan membuat staged pass manager lalu menjalankan metode `run`-nya dengan sirkuitmu sebagai input. Kamu bisa menggunakan fungsi [`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager#qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager) untuk menghasilkan staged pass manager dengan default yang wajar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More advanced users can customize a set of `PassManager` and `StagedPassManager` objects and determine the order in which each stage is run.  This can dramatically change the final output circuit. In fact, a custom approach to transpiling a quantum algorithm often produces more efficient error suppression than the default approach.  A custom approach involves rewriting quantum circuits to match hardware constraints and suppress the effects of noise.  The flow of logic for this tool chain is customizable and need not be linear.  The transpilation process can prepare iterative loops, conditional branches, and other complex behaviors.  A good starting place when developing a set of custom passes is to examine the default sequence of transformations.\n"
msgstr "Pengguna yang lebih mahir bisa mengkustomisasi sekumpulan objek `PassManager` dan `StagedPassManager` serta menentukan urutan setiap tahap dijalankan. Ini bisa mengubah sirkuit output akhir secara drastis. Bahkan, pendekatan kustom untuk melakukan transpilasi pada algoritma kuantum sering menghasilkan penekanan error yang lebih efisien dibanding pendekatan default. Pendekatan kustom melibatkan penulisan ulang sirkuit kuantum agar sesuai dengan batasan hardware dan menekan efek noise. Alur logika untuk toolchain ini dapat dikustomisasi dan tidak harus linear. Proses transpilasi bisa menyiapkan loop iteratif, cabang kondisional, dan perilaku kompleks lainnya. Titik awal yang bagus saat mengembangkan sekumpulan pass kustom adalah memeriksa urutan transformasi default.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an overview of transpiling using pass managers, see [Transpile with pass managers](transpile-with-pass-managers).\n"
msgstr "Untuk gambaran umum transpilasi menggunakan pass manager, lihat [Transpile with pass managers](transpile-with-pass-managers).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default transpilation {#default-transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilasi default {#default-transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a simpler, but less customizable, \"out-of-the-box\" way to use the transpiler, use the [`qiskit.compiler.transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#qiskit.compiler.transpile) function.  This generates and runs one of the preset `StagedPassManager` objects based on, among other options, an `optimization_level` flag that can be set to 0, 1, 2, or 3.  Higher levels generate more optimized circuits at the expense of longer transpilation times.\n"
msgstr "Untuk cara yang lebih sederhana namun kurang dapat dikustomisasi dalam menggunakan Transpiler secara \"langsung pakai\", gunakan fungsi [`qiskit.compiler.transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#qiskit.compiler.transpile). Ini menghasilkan dan menjalankan salah satu objek preset `StagedPassManager` berdasarkan, antara lain, flag `optimization_level` yang bisa diatur ke 0, 1, 2, atau 3. Level yang lebih tinggi menghasilkan sirkuit yang lebih optimal dengan biaya waktu transpilasi yang lebih lama.\n"

